# A program's own `check` (RULES.md, R213): a function of the name with a
# contract has its generated test, `contract of check`, which calls the
# prelude's `check` on its cases by a name the program cannot shadow, and
# calls the program's `check` as the function under test.
def check(level: int) -> bool:
    requires 0 <= level <= 10
    ensures result == (level > 5)
    return level > 5

def main():
    print(check(7))
    print(check(2))
